      "text": "Step 1: Identify the given information.\n- The initial conditions: a 2.28 liter container with a pressure of 5 kPa.\n- The final conditions: an 5.7 liter container at the same temperature.\n\nStep 2: Apply the inverse proportionality rule.\n- Since the pressure is inversely proportional to the volume, we have \\(P \\propto \\frac{1}{V}\\) or \\(P \\cdot V = k\\), where \\(k\\) is a constant.\n\nStep 3: Set up the equation with the initial and final conditions.\n- Initial condition: \\(P_1 = 5\\ kPa\\), \\(V_1 = 2.28\\ liters\\).\n- Final condition: \\(V_2 = 5.7\\ liters\\).\n\nStep 4: Solve for the constant \\(k\\).\n\\(P_1 \\cdot V_1 = k\\)\n\\(k = 5 \\times 2.28\\)\n\\(k = 11.4\\)\n\nStep 5: Use the constant \\(k\\) to find the final pressure.\n\\(P_2 \\cdot V_2 = k\\)\n\\(P_2 = \\frac{k}{V_2}\\)\n\\(P_2 = \\frac{11.4}{5.7}\\)\n\\(P_2 = 2\\ kPa\\)\n\nThe new pressure, when the volume changes to 5.7 liters, will be \\boxed{2} kPa.",
